From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hansen0411 <hansennguyen.ee14@nycu.edu.tw>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] HopCIM endpoint (hw/ip/hopcim) behind FuseSoC flags

- core-v-mini-mcu.core: flags use_cim, use_cim_ded, use_cim_mic, use_cim_mic5, use_cim_s,
  use_cim_mic4 (defines USE_CIM, CIM_FE_DED, USE_CIM_MIC, CIM_MIC_5M12, CIM_SEQ_S, CIM_MIC_4M096);
  depends on hopcim:ip:cim_endpoint (hw/ip/hopcim is a link to the HopCIM repository).
- hw/fpga/xilinx_core_v_mini_mcu_wrapper.sv: the endpoint on the CPU data master's external-slave
  port (a 1-to-1 tap); its PDM clock/data through x_heep_system; for use_cim_mic4 a BUFGCE that
  halves the 8.192 MHz MMCM output to 4.096 MHz.
- hw/system/x_heep_system.sv.tpl: ports cim_pdm_clk_i / cim_pdm_data_o (USE_CIM_MIC).
- tb/testharness.sv.tpl, tb/testharness_pkg.sv.tpl: the same tap in the Verilator SoC, so
  simulation and board see the same CPU-to-endpoint timing; a reserved 256 KiB window at
  0xC0040000 on the external bus. (Before this patch these lines existed only in the generated
  tb/testharness*.sv, which make mcu-gen overwrites.)
- tb/x-heep-tb-utils.core: depends on hopcim:ip:cim_endpoint under use_cim.
- vendored xheep_fpga_support: one clock-wizard fileset per flag (15 MHz stock, 15.36, 5.12,
  8.192 MHz) and their scripts; kept as hw/vendor/patches/xheep_fpga_support/0002-*.patch.
- sw/device/target/nexys-a7-100t/x-heep.h: REFERENCE_CLOCK_Hz can be set on the command line.
---
